PhoneNumberMetadata.xml — provenance and attribution
=====================================================

This file is copied VERBATIM from Google's libphonenumber project and is
the input to gen/generate.ae (which compiles a small subset of it into
../metadata.ae).

  Source:  https://github.com/google/libphonenumber
  File:    resources/PhoneNumberMetadata.xml
  URL:     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/libphonenumber/master/resources/PhoneNumberMetadata.xml
  Fetched: 2026-09-09

License
-------
libphonenumber is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Copyright (C) 2009 The Libphonenumber Authors.

The file retains its own Apache-2.0 copyright header (see the top of the
XML itself). The full license text is in ../reference/libphonenumber-LICENSE.

libphonenumber ships NO NOTICE file (verified: the repository has no
top-level NOTICE), so Apache-2.0 section 4(d) imposes no additional
notice-carrying obligation. This PROVENANCE file is our own attribution,
placed adjacent to the source as required by good practice and to record
where the file came from and when.

What we use
-----------
Only a small fraction. The generator reads six fields per territory for a
curated set of ~10 countries (id, country calling code, the fixedLine
possible-lengths, an example number, and one display format). The XML's
254 territories, per-type national-number regexes, leadingDigits routing,
and international-format templates are NOT consumed. See gen/generate.ae's
header for the exact scope and the isPossibleNumber-vs-isValidNumber note.
